"Design refinement (2026-08-12, user): PRESENCE IS REPLACED WITH INTIMIDATION, and intimidation is tied to ACTIONS rather than being fully passive. Every action -- even just moving -- carries an implicit intimidation against all enemies present, scaled by SIZE DIFFERENCE (the granular size stat; a kaiju stepping is terrifying, a fairy lunging is not). Morale still belongs to the faction side: when intimidation overwhelms the morale of everyone present in your faction, you are forced into the cowering stance (via the standard forced-stance contest machinery). RECOVERY LOOP: the cower stance carries a RALLY action that expends effort points (EP -- first real EP sink) to gain morale, and regained morale permits the stance change out of cowering. Notes: (a) this makes intimidation an ACTION FACET like the planned damage attributes -- actions carry rider payloads evaluated against bystanders, suggesting a shared 'action aura/rider' shape; (b) rally as a stance-granted action shows forced stances carrying their own counterplay, exactly the forced-stance customization design; (c) BLOCKING dependency (user): the morale system lands BEFORE fully populating the production action set, since every action's intimidation must be authored alongside it."